375	+# SMA-834 Anthropic open round with nested tool use — Implementation Plan
376	+
377	+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
378	+
379	+**Goal:** A tool-use-only `Item::AssistantMessage` inside an open tool round joins that round in the Anthropic translator, as an `Item::ToolCall` does.
380	+
381	+**Architecture:** One new branch in the `AssistantMessage` arm of `translate_messages`, before the current flush. A shared inner helper does "append to the last assistant message, or else queue", and the `ToolCall` arm and the new branch both call it.
382	+
383	+**Tech Stack:** Rust, `serde_json::Value` wire, `cargo test`.
384	+
385	+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-20-anthropic-open-round-nested-tool-use-design.md`
386	+
387	+## Global Constraints
388	+
389	+- Only `crates/paigasus-helikon-providers-anthropic/src/translate/request.rs` and `crates/paigasus-helikon-providers-anthropic/tests/live.rs` change.
390	+- No existing test changes. Every existing test stays green without edits.
391	+- No change to `round_is_answered`, `user_blocks`, or `assistant_blocks`.
392	+- Commit prefix: `<type>(providers): SMA-834 <lowercase message>`. Every commit message ends with a blank line and `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.
393	+- Before each commit: `cargo fmt --all` and `cargo clippy -p paigasus-helikon-providers-anthropic --all-features --all-targets -- -D warnings` are clean.
394	+- Work in the foreground. Do not background a cargo run. Do not stop before the command ends.
395	+- Do not run any git command that moves HEAD or switches the branch.
396	+
397	+## Review Focus
398	+
399	+1. A mixed message (text plus tool use) inside an open round must keep the flush. The parity test in Task 1 pins this.
400	+2. A message whose only non-tool parts are reasoning or blank text must join. The reasoning test in Task 1 pins this.
401	+3. A join into a run of adjacent assistant messages must go to the last message of the run. The adjacent-run test in Task 1 pins this.
402	+4. Two adjacent nested messages with no pending results must stay two messages. The existing test `round_spanning_adjacent_assistant_messages_is_not_split` pins this.
403	+5. An answered round must start a new round. `nested_tool_use_after_answered_round_starts_new_round` in Task 1 pins this.
404	+
